asi_Kapau_Selera_Minang.jpg","w":500,"h":359,"by":"Erisonjkambari","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nasi_Kapau_Selera_Minang.jpg"}},"ingredient/red-alga":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/red-alga","n":"Red alga","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Red algae, or Rhodophyta, make up one of the oldest and largest phyla of eukaryotic algae, containing over 7,000 recognized species within over 900 genera amidst ongoing taxonomic revisions. The majority of species (6,793) are in the class Florideophyceae, and mostly consist of multicellular marine algae, including many notable seaweeds. Red algae are abundant in marine habitats. Approximately 5% of red algae species occur in freshwater environments, with greater concentrations in warmer areas. This may be due to an evolutionary bottleneck in which the last common ancestor lost about 25% of its core genes and much of its evolutionary plasticity."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-red-alga"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_alga"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Nori","dish/nori"]]]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/fc/Sea_grapes_%28Botryocladia_pseudodichotoma%29_2.jpg/500px-Sea_grapes_%28Botryocladia_pseudodichotoma%29_2.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Coughdrop12","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sea_grapes_(Botryocladia_pseudodichotoma)_2.jpg"}},"dish/picarones":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/picarones","n":"Picarones","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Peruvian cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Picarones (or picarón singular) is a Peruvian dessert that originated in Lima during the viceroyalty. It is somewhat similar to buñuelos, a type of doughnut brought to the colonies by Spanish conquistadors. Its principal ingredients are squash and sweet potato. It is served in a doughnut form and covered with syrup, made from chancaca (solidified molasses). It is traditional to serve picarones when people prepare anticuchos, another traditional Peruvian dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-picarones"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picarones"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Peruvian cuisine","cuisine/peruvian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Chancaca","ingredient/chancaca"],["Cucurbita maxima","ingredient/cucurbita-maxima"],["Fig","ingredient/fig"],["Panela","ingredient/panela"],["Squash (plant)","ingredient/squash-plant"],["Sweet potato","ingredient/sweet-potato"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Peru Delights","ref":"site/perudelights-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"perudelights.com","note":"Morena Cuadra's blog of Peruvian home recipes and food culture.","url":"https://perudelights.com/tag/peruvian-home-cooking/","suggested":true},{"name":"Eat Peru","ref":"site/eatperu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"eatperu.com","note":"Guide to Peruvian dishes and ingredients with a recipe section.","url":"https://www.eatperu.com/category/recipes/?sf_paged=2","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Peruvian cuisine","links":[["Andina (restaurant)","dish/andina-restaurant"],["Anticucho","dish/anticucho"],["Central (restaurant)","dish/central-restaurant"],["Chicha morada","dish/chicha-morada"],["Coca tea","dish/coca-tea"],["La Rosa Náutica","dish/la-rosa-nautica"],["Lima (restaurant)","dish/lima-restaurant"],["Locro","dish/locro"],["Maido (restaurant)","dish/maido-restaurant"],["Peruvian ceviche","dish/peruvian-ceviche"],["Picantería","dish/picanteria"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/48/Peru_Picarones.jpg/500px-Peru_Picarones.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peru_Picarones.jpg"}},"dish/poached-egg":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/poached-egg","n":"Poached egg","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["A poached egg is an egg that has been cooked outside the shell by poaching (or sometimes steaming). This method of preparation can yield more delicately cooked eggs than higher temperature methods such as boiling. Poached eggs can be found in several dishes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-poached-egg"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poached_egg"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links"